{! layout("base") !}
{! block("title") !}Ecosystem — toke{! end !}
{! block("content") !}

<div class="page-hero">
  <h1>The <em>*oke</em> Ecosystem</h1>
  <p class="tagline">A layered stack of tools, frameworks, and runtimes — each named with the <code>*oke</code> convention. Four characters, always pronounceable, always part of the family.</p>
</div>

<div class="ecosystem-grid">

  <div class="oke-card oke-core">
    <div class="oke-badge">language</div>
    <h2><a href="/">toke</a></h2>
    <p>The core programming language, purpose-built for LLM code generation. 55-character syntax, zero runtime, single binary. Compiles via LLVM to native code on any platform.</p>
    <div class="oke-links">
      <a href="/docs">Docs</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="oke-card">
    <div class="oke-badge">web framework</div>
    <h2><a href="/ooke">ooke</a></h2>
    <p>A CMS and web framework built on toke. File-system routing, flat-file content store, template engine with Markdown, build and serve modes. Zero dependencies. Ships as a single binary. Serves tokelang.dev in production.</p>
    <div class="oke-links">
      <a href="/ooke">Project page</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/ooke">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="oke-card">
    <div class="oke-badge">intelligence layer</div>
    <h2><a href="/loke">loke</a></h2>
    <p>A locally-run intelligence layer that sits between users, their data, and external LLMs. 172 modules, 80,000+ lines of toke. Multi-layer PII detection, token optimisation, intelligent routing. 60–80% token reduction, all processing on-device.</p>
    <div class="oke-links">
      <a href="/loke">Project page</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/loke">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="oke-card oke-reserved">
    <div class="oke-badge">human experience</div>
    <h2>aoke</h2>
    <p>The topmost layer. Sound, light, perception — the interface between computation and the senses. UX, design systems, accessibility, and sensory analytics.</p>
    <div class="oke-meta">Reserved</div>
  </div>

  <div class="oke-card oke-reserved">
    <div class="oke-badge">hardware layer</div>
    <h2>zoke</h2>
    <p>The bottommost layer. Silicon, electrons, circuits — the physical substrate of computation. Drivers, ISA, FPGA, and everything below the OS.</p>
    <div class="oke-meta">Reserved</div>
  </div>

  <div class="oke-card">
    <div class="oke-badge">demo application</div>
    <h2>moke</h2>
    <p>A data analysis demo exercising loke's privacy pipeline, governance controls, and LLM integration. 26-detector analysis engine, 9 Australian-themed datasets, client-side ML. Integrated into the loke project.</p>
    <div class="oke-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/loke">GitHub (in loke)</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="ecosystem-note">
  <h3>The <em>*oke</em> naming convention</h3>
  <p>Every tool in the toke ecosystem uses a single consonant prefix followed by <code>oke</code>. Four characters, always pronounceable. The alphabetical ordering maps roughly to abstraction depth — <code>zoke</code> at the hardware layer, <code>aoke</code> at the human experience layer — giving the stack a built-in mnemonic.</p>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- The *oke Namespace                                             -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<div class="namespace-section">
  <h2>The <em>*oke</em> Namespace</h2>
  <p class="namespace-intro">26 letters, one naming convention. The full <code>*oke</code> alphabet maps to a layered architecture — from hardware physics at the bottom to human experience at the top.</p>

  <!-- Layer diagram -->
  <div class="layer-diagram">
    <div class="layer layer-top">
      <div class="layer-name">aoke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Human experience — perception, UX, light, sound</div>
      <div class="layer-tag">topmost</div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-connector"></div>
    <div class="layer layer-mid">
      <div class="layer-name">loke &nbsp; moke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Intelligence — AI/ML, privacy, data analysis</div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-connector"></div>
    <div class="layer layer-mid">
      <div class="layer-name">ooke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Web and middleware — static sites, routing, content</div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-connector"></div>
    <div class="layer layer-core">
      <div class="layer-name">toke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Core language — compiler, runtime, stdlib</div>
      <div class="layer-tag">core</div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-connector"></div>
    <div class="layer layer-mid">
      <div class="layer-name">woke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Governance — principles, licensing, values charter</div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-connector"></div>
    <div class="layer layer-bottom">
      <div class="layer-name">zoke</div>
      <div class="layer-desc">Hardware physics — silicon, electrons, circuits</div>
      <div class="layer-tag">bottommost</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Full alphabet table -->
  <h3 class="ns-table-heading">All 26 letters</h3>

  <div class="ns-group">
    <h4 class="ns-group-label"><span class="ns-badge ns-assigned">Assigned</span> 7 names in active use</h4>
    <table class="ns-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Role</th><th>Traditional equivalent</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>aoke</code></td><td>Human experience physics</td><td>UX, design systems, accessibility</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code class="ns-highlight">loke</code></td><td>Intelligence layer</td><td>LangChain, vector DB, RAG pipeline</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>moke</code></td><td>Demo application</td><td>Reference app, integration tests</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code class="ns-highlight">ooke</code></td><td>Web framework and SSG</td><td>Next.js, Django, Rails</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code class="ns-core">toke</code></td><td>Core programming language</td><td>Rust, Go, TypeScript</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>woke</code></td><td>Principles charter</td><td>OSS governance, Apache/CNCF</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>zoke</code></td><td>Fundamental compute physics</td><td>Hardware, drivers, ISA, FPGA</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="ns-group">
    <h4 class="ns-group-label"><span class="ns-badge ns-reserved">Reserved</span> 12 names held for future use</h4>
    <table class="ns-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Proposed role</th><th>Traditional equivalent</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>doke</code></td><td>Data / state management</td><td>Redux, Zustand, signals</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>hoke</code></td><td>Mock / test framework</td><td>Jest, Vitest, mocks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ioke</code></td><td>I/O and integrations</td><td>API clients, SDKs</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>joke</code></td><td>Easter eggs and fun</td><td>Developer experience / DX</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>koke</code></td><td>Performance and benchmarking</td><td>Profiling, APM, observability</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>noke</code></td><td>Networking / node layer</td><td>HTTP, service mesh, nginx</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>qoke</code></td><td>Queue / message layer</td><td>RabbitMQ, Kafka, SQS</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>roke</code></td><td>Caching / ephemeral storage</td><td>Redis, Memcached, CDN edge</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>soke</code></td><td>Auth / governance / permissions</td><td>OAuth, RBAC, JWT</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>voke</code></td><td>Virtualisation / containers</td><td>Docker, Wasm, VM isolation</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>xoke</code></td><td>Extensions / plugin system</td><td>LSP, WASI, kernel modules</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>yoke</code></td><td>Binding / orchestration</td><td>Kubernetes, Terraform, systemd</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="ns-group">
    <h4 class="ns-group-label"><span class="ns-badge ns-open">Open</span> 3 names available</h4>
    <table class="ns-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>eoke</code></td><td>Clean. Could suit events or streaming.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>foke</code></td><td>Clean. Sounds like "folk" — could suit community features.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uoke</code></td><td>Clean. Could suit utilities or stdlib.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="ns-group">
    <h4 class="ns-group-label"><span class="ns-badge ns-avoided">Avoided</span> 4 names permanently excluded</h4>
    <table class="ns-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>boke</code></td><td>Japanese for "idiot/fool" — globally known via anime and manzai comedy.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>coke</code></td><td>Coca-Cola trademark and drug slang. Both associations unusable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>goke</code></td><td>Too close to a serious racial slur. Proximity makes it unusable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>poke</code></td><td>Overloaded English verb, Facebook feature, Pokemon overlap. SEO-hostile.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

{! end !}
